        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 36px;">Introduction</h1>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
            <div style="width: 50%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Features</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Continuous supervision of trip circuit</li>
                    <li>Independent of the circuit breaker position</li>
                    <li>Low burden on auxiliary source</li>
                    <li>Complete range of rated AC / DC voltage</li>
                    <li>Operation indication for trip circuit health and unhealthiness</li>
                    <li>Low-level measuring current enables application of relay for high burden circuits</li>
                    <li>Supervision operation to avoid spurious signals during circuit breaker operation</li>
                    <li>Galvanic isolation between auxiliary supply and supervision circuit</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 50%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Applications</h3>
                <p>In a protection system the tripping of circuit breaker is crucial to build an interruption circuit in the power system. The supervision of the trip circuit is necessary to ensure that the trip circuit is properly functioning. The supervision function is particularly important when there is only one tripping coil. CB tripping is vital, for instance, for protection against short circuits or other transient circuit breaker in distribution networks. The supervision relay type TCS is intended for a continuous supervision of circuit breaker trip circuit and gives an alarm for loss of auxiliary supply, faults on the trip coil or its wiring, independent of the breaker position, faults on the supervision relay itself.</p>
                <p>The relay supports functions as indicated in Table 2.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
